Go net/http (Go 1.22+). The unmatched-route handler is the pattern "/" (lowest precedence in ServeMux): it answers 404, or 410 for retired paths, using the normal layout so the nav and home link are present (UX-005). Pages are rendered into a buffer first, so the status is chosen before any body byte is written and a template error can never leave a 200 with half a page. layout.html defines the "head" and "foot" every page uses, so the nav and home link are on every page, error pages included; 500.html, 503.html and 502.html have the same shape as 410.html (change the define name and the text). A database failure becomes 503, never 404 and never a 200 shell; a panic becomes a plain 500 page with no stack trace in the response (SEC-007).
