Go net/http (Go 1.22+; http.CrossOriginProtection needs Go 1.25, see the note in the code). A plain HTML form posting to a handler: it works without JavaScript, redirects (303) to a thank-you state only after the downstream call succeeded, and answers 502 when delivery fails. Run `go get golang.org/x/time/rate`. 502.html comes from the error-pages recipe. Set FORM_WEBHOOK_URL (your CRM, form provider or mail API). The in-memory limiter is per process (use Redis when you run several and trust X-Forwarded-For only behind your own proxy). Add Cloudflare Turnstile (`cf-turnstile-response`, verified server-side) if bots get past the honeypot.
